# Form controls

`Select` is a custom listbox (`SelectMenu`), not a native `<select>`. Chrome's
option popup ignores page and modal scale. The menu portals to `document.body`
so modal `overflow` does not clip it. Items use `text-base` and 44px taps
below `lg` (`text-sm` on desktop).

`YearSelect` is a typed year field (`inputMode="numeric"`), not a listbox.
Non-digits are stripped as you type (max four digits). The committed year
must fall in `[from, to]`, the same range the old dropdown listed; out of
range (or a required empty) shows `Enter a year between {min} and {max}`
and does not write. Clearing an `allowEmpty` field yields `undefined`.
Parse / strip helpers live in `yearInput.ts`.

`ComboInput` stays a text field with in-flow suggestions. Enter on a
highlighted suggestion is still ignored by `submitEditOnEnter` (preventDefault).
